;; julia-professional-registry_chora.deed — the repo deed (standards 1-formats/deed).
;;
;; One deed per repo (standards #837, owner ruling 2026-09-19, Option A). This
;; registry was instantiated from hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo but never had
;; the deed/k9 half of that template applied, so it was the outlier among the
;; 210 estate repos that carry a <repo>_chora.deed. Adding it is a conformance
;; fix, not a redesign.
;;
;; Deliberately MINIMAL, on the same pattern as hyperpolymath/verisimdb's deed
;; rather than the template's own exhaustive 1100-line record. Two reasons:
;;   1. An archetype/template-derived record "must not write fiction"
;;      (rsr-template-repo archetypes/README.adoc) — so no clause appears here
;;      that cannot be read off a file in this repo.
;;   2. The (canon) clause pins canon.lock artefact hashes. A guessed pin is
;;      worse than no pin: standards' check-canon-lockstep.sh compares it
;;      against canon.lock and a wrong hash is a hard failure. The pin belongs
;;      in a change that runs that check, not in a conformance commit.
;;
;; Read any field with: scripts/deed-field.sh <field>
;; Grammar: standards 1-formats/deed/spec/abnf/deed.abnf
(repo-deed
  :schema-version "1.0.0"
  :canonical-name "julia-professional-registry"
  :repo-uuid #u5"github.com/hyperpolymath/julia-professional-registry"
  (status
    :present #t
    :ended #f
    :note "Hyperpolymath Julia package registry: the estate's own Pkg registry (Registry.toml, uuid 2ba92a00-ca78-4729-9a29-51b4a830c8fa), 41 packages resolved through it by URL in consumer CI."))
